      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "* preventing DOC from exercising necessary discretion in using effective de-escalation practices for the purpose of calming disruptive individuals and victims of violence, in that Local Law 42 inflexibly and arbitrarily restricts the maximum duration of de-escalation confinement to four hours, even though circumstances sometimes arise in which a longer stay is necessary for safety, and it inflexibly mandates that persons in de-escalation confinement be allowed to make phone calls outside the facility, notwithstanding that it is dangerous and unsound correctional policy for a person who has engaged in a violent fight, particularly if the fight is gang-related, to be able to telephone their confederates to spread the word [Dkt. No. 758-1 at para. 30-33]; and",
